    id:"astronuclear",
    title:"Astronuclear engineering",
    html:"<p>The <a href='westinghouse-astronuclear-laboratory.html'>Westinghouse Astronuclear Laboratory</a> applies the corporation's reactor, turbine, generator, control, and materials businesses to spacecraft propulsion. It develops the nuclear subsystem for Aerojet-General's NERVA engine and later works on nuclear-electric power conversion and large orbit-assembled propulsion structures.</p><p>Astronuclear work remains a specialist division inside the larger electrical company. Its exact postwar corporate organization is open.</p>"
